{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfvah1R5nYTLonK8WBpUs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Recommendation: don't commission the diary study as framed. Set a default of retiring the widget, and run a short, cheap check that could overturn it.**\n\n**Why**\n- The evidence so far points to low value. Adoption is 1.1%, and retention matches matched non-users, so there's no sign it earns its keep.\n- The cost is real and recurring: about three QA days per iOS release, plus a five-week rewrite. That's likely over six engineer-weeks in the next year for a feature with no measured benefit.\n- A diary study mostly tells you what widget users want. Your decision is whether any widget is worth keeping at all. It's slow, it samples a self-selected 1.1%, and it can't tell you whether a widget could matter to the other 99%.\n- The matched comparison is weak. If the widget helps the users who rely on it, an average null result could hide that. That's the question worth checking, and it needs data, not diaries.\n\n**Cheap check (about a week, existing data only)**\n1. Do widget users log habits from the widget, or only view it? How often?\n2. Does retention differ for heavy widget users? Do the users who add it come from a segment that already retains well?\n3. Are widgets a frequent request in reviews or support tickets?\n4. Does the widget feed any engagement or revenue metric you care about?\n\n**Decision rule, set in advance**\n- If none of these shows a meaningful signal, retire it. Warn current users in-app well before the API deadline.\n- If there's a clear signal, such as heavy users who log from it and retain better, scope a smaller rewrite. Cut QA cost with automated widget tests, then run a narrow diary study on those users.\n\nEither way, set a decision date that leaves at least five weeks, plus buffer, before Apple's cutoff."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3449,"cache_read_input_tokens":5037,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3449},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ec037cff-09fc-47ef-80cc-d861e69e649e","uuid":"63acc150-4890-46be-a724-17f0f7f16a7f","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:08:55.973Z","request_id":"req_011Cfvah1ATUvmdwR96N1QFh"}
